# Sprint 2 Planning Notes & Sprint 1 Retro Follow-Up

**Project:** Hope, Inc. ERP System (`INFOMAN`)  
**Sprint:** Sprint 2 (Weeks 3–4)  
**Scrum Master:** Jemirol Arbado  

## Sprint 2 Goal
Consolidate authentication and core UI screens into a unified frontend structure (`index.html`), implement password recovery UI (`reset-password.html`), and enforce standardized GitHub issue/PR tracking across all roles.

## Follow-Up on Sprint 1 Retrospective Actions (`-02`)
- [x] **Standardized Branching & PR Workflow:** Established branch naming conventions (`feature/...`, `fix/...`, `docs/...`) and required linked issues before merging.
- [x] **Repository Documentation Structure:** Centralized all Scrum artifacts inside `/docs` and updated `README.md` with clear setup and contribution guidelines.
- [x] **Issue & Sub-Issue Tracking:** Broken down large features (e.g., Password Reset `#93` → `#94`) to separate completed frontend layouts from upcoming Supabase backend tasks.

## Sprint 2 Backlog Assignments
- **UI/UX Designer:** Empty, error, and confirm-delete states; usability review of built screens.
- **Developers:** Unified `index.html` auth view consolidation, `reset-password.html` layout, and registration password field validation (`#97`).
- **QA / Tester:** Functional verification of login, registration, and password reset flows.
- **Scrum Master:** Sprint 2 board setup, impediment tracking, velocity/burndown updates, and Sprint 2 Review/Retrospective documentation.
